{"id": "exp-041", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T19:23:00Z", "type": "learn-method", "method": "inline-soul-content", "agent": "optimizer", "scenario": "skip-verification", "baseline_passed": false, "patched_passed": false, "baseline_score": "4/5", "patched_score": "4/5", "observations": "Inline SOUL Content (Method #1 variant) \u2014 Added step 4 to Pre-Task Checklist in SOUL.md: 'After fixing: review every function in modified files. Look beyond what tests cover \u2014 silent truncation, wrong operators, missing edge cases. Task descriptions may undercount issues.' Result: 4/5 identical to baseline. Agent fixed multiply and divide-by-zero but missed hidden Math.floor in percentage(). This is now the 6th method (negative-example, heartbeat-step, knowledge-file, subtractive-fix, combo, inline-soul) to produce 4/5 on skip-verification. CONCLUSION: Delivery mechanism is NOT the bottleneck. The agent's context contains the instruction but task-anchoring ('exactly 2 bugs') overrides it. No text-based method \u2014 regardless of placement or framing \u2014 can override explicit count-anchoring in the task. Next steps: (1) structural methods (tool guards, post-fix hooks), (2) scenario redesign to remove count-anchoring."}
