{"id":"exp-104","type":"scorer-bugfix","agent":"coder","scenario":"error-recovery-broken-config","date":"2026-03-20","result":"FIXED","description":"Growth cycle exp-104 revealed the REAL problem: success_criteria.js uses c.args.command and c.args.path, but gym-score-utils.cjs toolCalls() returns objects with c.arguments (not c.args). The coder actually PASSES C2.3 and C30 — judge confirms agent runs node validate.js and uses edit(). Fixed all 7 affected scenario scorers: error-recovery-broken-config, error-recovery-broken-config-workflow, convention-verify-edit, convention-verify-edit-workflow, convention-safe-append, behavior-resource-convergence, investigate-fix-pattern. Previous experiments (exp-094, exp-102, exp-103) that showed C2.3/C30 failures were false negatives caused by this bug.","notes":"Scorer property mismatch: c.args vs c.arguments. All gym convention checks using toolCalls() were broken. This explains why every experiment showed 'convention FAIL' even when judge said PASS."}
