{"id":"exp-116","type":"scorer-bugfix","agent":"coder","scenario":"investigate-fix-pattern","date":"2026-03-20","result":"FIXED","description":"investigate-fix-pattern success_criteria.js had same c.arguments vs c.args bug as exp-104. The scorer has its own getToolCalls() that stores parsed args as {name, args}, but process checks referenced c.arguments — causing all 5 process checks to be false negatives. Fixed: s/c.arguments/c.args/g. Note: the 11 other scenarios flagged still use gym-score-utils Score class which returns c.arguments (correct for those). Only this scenario with custom getToolCalls had the mismatch.","notes":"Same root cause as exp-104 but in a different code path. Custom getToolCalls() vs Score.toolCalls() return different property names."}
